Subject: [PATCH] Review: effects of activating the original book's
 sessionVaultFactory entry (read-only)

The contract rules (v1/v2 beneficialOwnerOf, _apply, _claim; SessionVault ownerCall
and release) show that a policy pinned to a SessionVault would be stranded by
activation. The state probe (one agreed block, 16 requests) reads every id in the
current ledger: 98 ids; 0 stranded policies in either vault. The 4 ids owned by
the admin's SessionVault have no policy, so only their first writer changes
(0xb794 -> 0x0b2d); the existing 0x4e62 policies are EOA-owned and unchanged.
Bounded, resumable log discovery (2 attempts, <=20 requests each, exact topics)
covered 52605914-52728413 on the only allowlisted archive-log provider (5000-block
limit); 52728414-52999031 is recorded as uncovered.
CONSUMERS.md lists every runtime reader of the key; the relay's SESSIONS_FACTORY
setting is not determined from public evidence. No transaction, key or SSH.
